- Because they are weak symbols, existing code that already provides its own definitions will still override them; however, our definitions are placed in a separate object file that is linked **before** any user code that might provide its own definitions.
- Using **LD\_PRELOAD** ensures the wrapper runs in every process that loads it, giving you visibility into all allocations performed by your program.
